@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `bmfire-nouns`
IMPORT `bmfire-insuring-clause`
IMPORT `bmfire-conditions`
IMPORT `bmfire-claim`
IMPORT `bmfire-fixtures`

-- LAYER 3 TESTS: what each party must do, and by when, and what a failure costs. The
-- expected values are the Rules' own periods (7 days, 30 days, 30 days empty, 2 months,
-- 12 months, the short-period scale), tested on both sides of each edge. The standard case
-- (bmfire-fixtures.l4) is a fire on 1 June 2026, every condition met, written claim on
-- 11 June, premium accepted 1 January and paid 10 January.

§ `Tests — conditions and duties`

§§ `The conditions on the claim file`

GIVEN ls IS A LIST OF `A lapse in a test`
GIVETH A `The claim`
`the standard fire, with` ls MEANS
    `a claim in full` `the Summary` `risk A` `the day` (`the facts` `fire`)
        (LIST (`at the insured location` "Hanoi" (LIST (`physical damage to` `the building` `of` 200000000 `with` EMPTY))))
        `the premium paid on 10 January 2026` EMPTY EMPTY EMPTY (`conduct` (YMD 2026 6 11) ls) FALSE 0

GIVEN l IS A `A lapse in a test`
GIVETH A LIST OF `A reason a claim or a loss is not covered`
`the reasons with the lapse` l MEANS `the reasons the whole claim fails` (`the standard fire, with` (LIST l))

#ASSERT `the reasons the whole claim fails` (`the standard fire, with` EMPTY) EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT `the reasons with the lapse` `lapse — misdeclared, misdescribed, gave untrue information, or did not disclose material information about the insured risk` EQUALS LIST `VI.2 — the policy is void for misdeclaration or non-disclosure`
#ASSERT `the reasons with the lapse` `lapse — not: kept the insured property in good repair and took every proper measure to prevent DAMAGE` EQUALS LIST `VI.6 — the property was not kept in good repair, or DAMAGE not guarded against`
#ASSERT `the reasons with the lapse` `lapse — not: took steps at once to minimise the loss and recover lost property` EQUALS LIST `VII.1(a)(i) — no steps taken at once to minimise the loss`
#ASSERT `the reasons with the lapse` `lapse — not: notified Bao Minh in writing at once` EQUALS LIST `VII.1(a)(ii) — Bao Minh not notified in writing at once`
#ASSERT `the reasons with the lapse` `lapse — not: supplied at its own expense the information and documents Bao Minh reasonably required, with a sworn statement` EQUALS LIST `VII.1 — the information and documents required were not supplied`
#ASSERT `the reasons with the lapse` `lapse — the claim was fraudulent` EQUALS LIST `VII.2(a) — fraud, or a wilful act or connivance of the Insured`
#ASSERT `the reasons with the lapse` `lapse — the Insured, or anyone on its behalf, used fraudulent means to benefit under the policy` EQUALS LIST `VII.2(a) — fraud, or a wilful act or connivance of the Insured`
#ASSERT `the reasons with the lapse` `lapse — the DAMAGE was caused by a wilful act, or with the connivance, of the Insured` EQUALS LIST `VII.2(a) — fraud, or a wilful act or connivance of the Insured`
#ASSERT `the reasons with the lapse` `lapse — not: did what Bao Minh required to enforce rights against third parties` EQUALS LIST `VII.7 — the steps required against third parties were not taken`
-- VII.3: the plans matter only where Bao Minh elected to repair or replace.
#ASSERT `the reasons with the lapse` `lapse — not: supplied the plans and information Bao Minh asked for to repair or replace` EQUALS EMPTY
`a repair Bao Minh elected, plans not supplied` MEANS
    `a claim in full` `the Summary` `risk A` `the day` (`the facts` `fire`)
        (LIST (`at the insured location` "Hanoi" (LIST (`physical damage to` `the building` `of` 200000000 `with` EMPTY))))
        `the premium paid on 10 January 2026` EMPTY EMPTY EMPTY (`conduct` (YMD 2026 6 11) (LIST `lapse — not: supplied the plans and information Bao Minh asked for to repair or replace`)) TRUE 0
#ASSERT `the reasons the whole claim fails` `a repair Bao Minh elected, plans not supplied` EQUALS LIST `VII.3 — the plans and information to repair or replace were not supplied`

-- VII.1(a)(iii): the police only where the damage was done by a deliberate act or sabotage.
#ASSERT `the reasons with the lapse` `lapse — not: notified the police at once` EQUALS EMPTY
GIVEN ls IS A LIST OF `A lapse in a test`
GIVETH A `The claim`
`an arson, with` ls MEANS
    `a claim in full` `the Summary` `risk A` `the day` (`the facts` (`fact — the damage was done by a deliberate act or by sabotage` FOLLOWED BY `fire`))
        (LIST (`at the insured location` "Hanoi" (LIST (`physical damage to` `the building` `of` 200000000 `with` EMPTY))))
        `the premium paid on 10 January 2026` EMPTY EMPTY EMPTY (`conduct` (YMD 2026 6 11) ls) FALSE 0
#ASSERT `the reasons the whole claim fails` (`an arson, with` EMPTY) EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT `the reasons the whole claim fails` (`an arson, with` (LIST `lapse — not: notified the police at once`)) EQUALS LIST `VII.1(a)(iii) — the police not notified at once`

-- "Ngay lập tức" has no number of days.
#ASSERT REFUSED `VII.1(a) — the number of days the Insured has to notify Bao Minh` BECAUSE "VII.1(a) — the Rules say at once and give no number of days"

§§ `VII.1(b) — thirty days, or longer if Bao Minh allows`

GIVEN d IS A DATE
      m IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF `A reason a claim or a loss is not covered`
`the reasons, written claim delivered on` d `with a longer period of` m MEANS
    `the reasons the whole claim fails`
        (`a claim in full` `the Summary` `risk A` `the day` (`the facts` `fire`)
            (LIST (`at the insured location` "Hanoi" (LIST (`physical damage to` `the building` `of` 200000000 `with` EMPTY))))
            `the premium paid on 10 January 2026` EMPTY EMPTY EMPTY (`conduct with a longer period` d m EMPTY) FALSE 0)

-- DAMAGE on 1 June; 1 June + 30 days = 1 July.
#ASSERT `the reasons, written claim delivered on` (YMD 2026 7 1) `with a longer period of` NOTHING EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT `the reasons, written claim delivered on` (YMD 2026 7 2) `with a longer period of` NOTHING EQUALS LIST `VII.1(b) — the written claim was not delivered in time`
-- Bao Minh allowed 45 days in writing: 16 July in time, 17 July late.
#ASSERT `the reasons, written claim delivered on` (YMD 2026 7 16) `with a longer period of` (JUST 45) EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT `the reasons, written claim delivered on` (YMD 2026 7 17) `with a longer period of` (JUST 45) EQUALS LIST `VII.1(b) — the written claim was not delivered in time`
-- A "longer" period that is shorter does not shorten the thirty days.
#ASSERT `the reasons, written claim delivered on` (YMD 2026 7 1) `with a longer period of` (JUST 20) EQUALS EMPTY

§§ `VI.3 — alteration and removal`

GIVEN k IS A `A kind of change under condition VI.3`
      d IS A DATE
      consented IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF `A reason a claim or a loss is not covered`
`the reasons after a change of kind` k `from` d `, consented` consented MEANS
    `the reasons the whole claim fails`
        (`a claim in full` `the Summary` `risk A` `the day` (`the facts` `fire`)
            (LIST (`at the insured location` "Hanoi" (LIST (`physical damage to` `the building` `of` 200000000 `with` EMPTY))))
            `the premium paid on 10 January 2026` EMPTY
            (LIST (`A change under condition VI.3` WITH `kind` IS k, `date it began` IS d, `Bao Minh consented by an endorsement before the DAMAGE` IS consented))
            EMPTY (`conduct` (YMD 2026 6 11) EMPTY) FALSE 0)

`a change of trade` MEANS `a change of trade or occupation, or another change, affecting the insured building or the insured property in it and increasing the likelihood of DAMAGE by an insured risk`
`left empty` MEANS `the insured building, or the building holding insured property, left empty`
#ASSERT `the reasons after a change of kind` `a change of trade` `from` (YMD 2026 5 1) `, consented` FALSE EQUALS LIST `VI.3 — the policy had ceased for the property lost`
#ASSERT `the reasons after a change of kind` `a change of trade` `from` (YMD 2026 5 1) `, consented` TRUE EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT `the reasons after a change of kind` `a change of trade` `from` (YMD 2026 6 2) `, consented` FALSE EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT `the reasons after a change of kind` `insured property moved to a building or location other than the one stated` `from` (YMD 2026 5 1) `, consented` FALSE EQUALS LIST `VI.3 — the policy had ceased for the property lost`
#ASSERT `the reasons after a change of kind` `the interest in insured property passed from the Insured to another, otherwise than by will or by operation of law` `from` (YMD 2026 5 1) `, consented` FALSE EQUALS LIST `VI.3 — the policy had ceased for the property lost`
-- (b) empty 30 days or more: from 2 May, 30 days to 1 June; from 3 May, 29.
#ASSERT `the reasons after a change of kind` `left empty` `from` (YMD 2026 5 2) `, consented` FALSE EQUALS LIST `VI.3 — the policy had ceased for the property lost`
#ASSERT `the reasons after a change of kind` `left empty` `from` (YMD 2026 5 3) `, consented` FALSE EQUALS EMPTY

§§ `VI.5 — warranties`

GIVEN renewal IS A BOOLEAN
      ws      IS A LIST OF `A warranty`
      ls      IS A LIST OF `A lapse in a test`
GIVETH A LIST OF `A reason a claim or a loss is not covered`
`the reasons, renewal` renewal `warranties` ws `lapses` ls MEANS
    `the reasons the whole claim fails`
        (`a claim in full` (`a 2026 Summary in full` `every risk` 1500000000 EMPTY FALSE FALSE renewal) `risk A` `the day` (`the facts` `fire`)
            (LIST (`at the insured location` "Hanoi" (LIST (`physical damage to` `the building` `of` 200000000 `with` EMPTY))))
            `the premium paid on 10 January 2026` EMPTY EMPTY ws (`conduct` (YMD 2026 6 11) ls) FALSE 0)

`a sprinkler warranty, not kept` MEANS `A warranty` WITH `description` IS "sprinklers maintained", `not complied with during the period of insurance` IS TRUE
`a sprinkler warranty, kept` MEANS `A warranty` WITH `description` IS "sprinklers maintained", `not complied with during the period of insurance` IS FALSE
#ASSERT `the reasons, renewal` TRUE `warranties` (LIST `a sprinkler warranty, not kept`) `lapses` EMPTY EQUALS LIST `VI.5 — a warranty was not complied with`
#ASSERT `the reasons, renewal` TRUE `warranties` (LIST `a sprinkler warranty, kept`) `lapses` EMPTY EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT `the reasons, renewal` TRUE `warranties` EMPTY `lapses` (LIST `lapse — insured the deductible during the period of the policy`) EQUALS LIST `VI.5 — a warranty was not complied with`
-- A first period, not a renewal: on the text, no bar (finding X6).
#ASSERT `the reasons, renewal` FALSE `warranties` (LIST `a sprinkler warranty, not kept`) `lapses` EMPTY EQUALS EMPTY

§§ `VIII.3 — the premium payment warranty`

GIVEN p IS A `The premium`
      d IS A DATE
      es IS A LIST OF `An endorsement`
GIVETH A LIST OF `A reason a claim or a loss is not covered`
`the reasons, premium` p `DAMAGE on` d `endorsements` es MEANS
    `the reasons the whole claim fails`
        (`a claim in full` `the Summary` `risk A` d (`the facts` `fire`)
            (LIST (`at the insured location` "Hanoi" (LIST (`physical damage to` `the building` `of` 200000000 `with` EMPTY))))
            p es EMPTY EMPTY (`conduct` (d PLUS 10) EMPTY) FALSE 0)

-- Accepted 1 January: 30 days to 31 January.
#ASSERT `the reasons, premium` (`a premium paid on` (JUST (YMD 2026 1 31))) `DAMAGE on` (YMD 2026 6 1) `endorsements` EMPTY EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT `the reasons, premium` (`a premium paid on` (JUST (YMD 2026 2 1))) `DAMAGE on` (YMD 2026 6 1) `endorsements` EMPTY EQUALS LIST `VIII.3.2 — the cover was cancelled for unpaid premium before the DAMAGE`
-- Never paid: DAMAGE within the 30 days stays covered (clause 2, fork F27); after, not.
#ASSERT `the reasons, premium` (`a premium paid on` NOTHING) `DAMAGE on` (YMD 2026 1 20) `endorsements` EMPTY EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT `the reasons, premium` (`a premium paid on` NOTHING) `DAMAGE on` (YMD 2026 1 31) `endorsements` EMPTY EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT `the reasons, premium` (`a premium paid on` NOTHING) `DAMAGE on` (YMD 2026 2 1) `endorsements` EMPTY EQUALS LIST `VIII.3.2 — the cover was cancelled for unpaid premium before the DAMAGE`

-- (b) instalments: the first within 30 days of acceptance, the rest on their agreed days.
GIVEN `second paid` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A `The premium`
`two instalments, the second paid on` `second paid` MEANS
    `The premium` WITH
        `date cover was accepted`                  IS YMD 2026 1 1
        `Bao Minh accepted payment in instalments` IS TRUE
        `date the premium was paid in full`        IS NOTHING
        `instalments`                              IS LIST (`An instalment of premium` WITH `agreed date` IS YMD 2026 1 15, `date paid` IS JUST (YMD 2026 1 25)),
                                                           (`An instalment of premium` WITH `agreed date` IS YMD 2026 4 1, `date paid` IS `second paid`)
        `an agreed premium payment term, in days`  IS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the reasons, premium` (`two instalments, the second paid on` (JUST (YMD 2026 4 1))) `DAMAGE on` (YMD 2026 6 1) `endorsements` EMPTY EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT `the reasons, premium` (`two instalments, the second paid on` NOTHING) `DAMAGE on` (YMD 2026 6 1) `endorsements` EMPTY EQUALS LIST `VIII.3.2 — the cover was cancelled for unpaid premium before the DAMAGE`
#ASSERT `the reasons, premium` (`two instalments, the second paid on` NOTHING) `DAMAGE on` (YMD 2026 3 15) `endorsements` EMPTY EQUALS EMPTY

-- (c) an agreed payment term under 30 days: within the period of insurance.
`a 15-day term, never paid` MEANS
    `The premium` WITH
        `date cover was accepted`                  IS YMD 2026 1 1
        `Bao Minh accepted payment in instalments` IS FALSE
        `date the premium was paid in full`        IS NOTHING
        `instalments`                              IS EMPTY
        `an agreed premium payment term, in days`  IS JUST 15
#ASSERT `VIII.3.1 — the last day to pay the premium, or its first instalment` `a 15-day term, never paid` `the Summary` EQUALS YMD 2026 12 31
#ASSERT `the reasons, premium` `a 15-day term, never paid` `DAMAGE on` (YMD 2026 6 1) `endorsements` EMPTY EQUALS EMPTY

-- Endorsements: 30 days from the later of issue and effect.
GIVEN i IS A DATE
      e IS A DATE
      p IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH AN `An endorsement`
`an endorsement issued` i `effective` e `paid` p MEANS
    `An endorsement` WITH `date of issue` IS i, `date its cover takes effect` IS e, `date its premium was paid in full` IS p
#ASSERT `VIII.3.1(a)(ii)-(iii) — the last day to pay an endorsement's premium` (`an endorsement issued` (YMD 2026 3 1) `effective` (YMD 2026 3 15) `paid` NOTHING) EQUALS YMD 2026 4 14
#ASSERT `VIII.3.1(a)(ii)-(iii) — the last day to pay an endorsement's premium` (`an endorsement issued` (YMD 2026 3 1) `effective` (YMD 2026 3 1) `paid` NOTHING) EQUALS YMD 2026 3 31
#ASSERT `VIII.3.1(a)(ii)-(iii) — the last day to pay an endorsement's premium` (`an endorsement issued` (YMD 2026 3 1) `effective` (YMD 2026 2 1) `paid` NOTHING) EQUALS YMD 2026 3 31
#ASSERT `the reasons, premium` `the premium paid on 10 January 2026` `DAMAGE on` (YMD 2026 6 1) `endorsements` (LIST (`an endorsement issued` (YMD 2026 3 1) `effective` (YMD 2026 3 15) `paid` NOTHING)) EQUALS LIST `VIII.3.2 — an endorsement relied on was cancelled for unpaid premium before the DAMAGE`
#ASSERT `the reasons, premium` `the premium paid on 10 January 2026` `DAMAGE on` (YMD 2026 6 1) `endorsements` (LIST (`an endorsement issued` (YMD 2026 3 1) `effective` (YMD 2026 3 15) `paid` (JUST (YMD 2026 4 14)))) EQUALS EMPTY

§§ `VI.4 — cancellation, and the short-period scale`

-- Bao Minh's notice issued 2 July 2026 takes effect 9 July. Refund from the notice day:
-- 12,000,000 x (2 July to 31 December, 182 days) / (1 January to 31 December, 364 days)
-- = 6,000,000.
#ASSERT `VI.4 — the day Bao Minh's cancellation takes effect` (YMD 2026 7 2) EQUALS YMD 2026 7 9
#ASSERT `VI.4 — the premium Bao Minh refunds when it cancels` `the Summary` (YMD 2026 7 2) EQUALS 6000000

-- The Insured's notice given 25 March takes effect 1 April.
#ASSERT `VI.4 — the day the Insured's termination takes effect` (YMD 2026 3 25) EQUALS YMD 2026 4 1

