-- A policy whose premium for the period (3,000,000) is below 30% of the annual premium
-- (12,000,000): the Rules do not say whether the Insured owes the 600,000 difference.
`a short policy` MEANS
    `The Policy Summary` WITH
        `start of the period of insurance`                               IS YMD 2026 1 1
        `end of the period of insurance`                                 IS YMD 2026 3 31
        `risks stated as insured`                                        IS LIST `risk A`
        `total sum insured`                                              IS 1000000000
        `deductibles stated`                                             IS EMPTY
        `premium for the period of insurance`                            IS 3000000
        `annual premium`                                                 IS 12000000
        `rent insured under this policy`                                 IS FALSE
        `Bao Minh agreed to reinstate the sums insured already paid out` IS FALSE
        `a renewal of an earlier period`                                 IS FALSE
#ASSERT REFUSED `VI.4 — the premium returned when the Insured ends the policy` `a short policy` (YMD 2026 2 1) BECAUSE "VI.4 — the Rules do not say whether the Insured owes the excess of the short-period premium over the premium for the period"

§§ `VII.2(b) — twelve months to sue`

-- Rejected 15 March 2026: the twelve months end 15 March 2027.
